{"name":"Corky","hex":"#bd9b78","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"corky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of wine, contaminated by a faulty or tainted cork.","Consisting of, or like, cork; dry; shrivelled."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep bruise, usually on the leg or buttock, caused by a blow; a haematoma."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corky Ballas","blocks":[{"text":"Mark Alexander \"Corky\" Ballas Sr. is an American retired competitive ballroom dancer who holds several Latin dance championship titles. His son, Mark Ballas, is a professional dancer on Dancing with the Stars. His father was George Ballas, who invented the Weed Eater lawn-trimming device."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corky_Ballas"},{"title":"Corky (orca)","blocks":[{"text":"Corky II, often referred to as just Corky, is a female captive orca from the A5 Pod of northern resident orcas. At approximately the age of four, Corky was captured from Pender Harbour off the coast of British Columbia on 11 December 1969. She has lived at SeaWorld San Diego in San Diego, California since 21 January 1987. As of 2024, she is the oldest and longest kept captive orca. SeaWorld San Diego celebrates her birthday on January 1 every year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Shamubeach.jpg/330px-Shamubeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corky_(orca)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Shamubeach.jpg/500px-Shamubeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Shamubeach.jpg/1280px-Shamubeach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Shamubeach.jpg/500px-Shamubeach.jpg?ut